    author_source: asserted
notes[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-26T13:52:41.808Z",codex,"Baseline measured 2026-07-26 with Node built-in coverage against the latest project-local pm CLI: dist/index.js 82.84% lines, 74.67% branches, 92.19% functions. The aggregate report is lower because it also observes a temporary installed extension copy; the source file row is the actionable baseline."
  "2026-07-26T14:13:07.264Z",codex,"Workflow-level acceptance evidence is now linked in addition to the reporting-only coverage baseline. This Issue remains open until release:check itself enforces all four 100% thresholds; a passing current release:check is not evidence that the acceptance criteria are met."
  "2026-08-02T00:42:20.038Z","harness:codex","TDD tranche 1: added a real registered-command acceptance matrix covering all nine command families, host-global JSON, Slack/JSON/Markdown output, output-file persistence, real PM reads, duplicate/governance SDK scans, activity deltas, and Git divergence. Targeted test passes. Full suite now passes 161 tests and source coverage improved from 91.97/76.72/95.85 to 94.86% lines, 78.71% branches, and 96.27% functions. The issue remains in progress; thresholds are intentionally unchanged until meaningful tests reach exact 100/100/100."
  "2026-08-07T07:30:38.541Z","harness:codex","TDD tranche 2 on release head v2026.08.07: rebased the registered-command acceptance matrix onto current main; removed two zero-use production helpers; added behavior-driven coverage for text ranking with confidence and explanations,typed focus parsing,staleness and momentum text output,invalid positive and non-negative integer flags,default-branch discovery through local main and origin/HEAD,and deterministic ordering across multiple real SDK duplicate clusters. The suite now covers 294/294 functions (100%),4383/4547 lines (96.39%),and 1148/1434 branches (80.06%). @unbrained/pm-cli resolves to latest 2026.8.6 and pm-changelog to latest 2026.8.7. Exact line/branch coverage remains open; thresholds intentionally remain at the existing ratchet until genuine behavior reaches 100/100/100."
  "2026-08-07T07:37:01.435Z","harness:codex","CI round 1 found a runner-topology assumption in the new acceptance matrix: actions/checkout leaves a detached HEAD without a local main ref,so the clean divergence fixture failed before later command cases ran. Production correctly rejected the unknown ref. The fixture now compares HEAD with HEAD,preserving the clean-divergence contract without assuming branch refs. Targeted registered-command test and typecheck pass."
  "2026-08-07T07:39:30.482Z","harness:codex","Review round 1 accepted three CodeRabbit findings: the privacy blocker now links explicit future fail-closed identity and all-ref content audit commands; typed-focus and ID-focus are independent behavioral assertions; and origin/HEAD points to trunk so its resolution cannot pass through the main fallback. The privacy commands are acceptance contracts and are not claimed green while the published-history blocker remains open."
files[2]{path,scope,note}:
  index.ts,project,Source coverage target
  test/brief.test.ts,project,Coverage test expansion
tests[2]{command,path,scope,timeout_seconds}:
  "NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG=/dev/null npm run release:check",.github/workflows/ci.yml,project,1800
  "npm run build && npm run build:test && node --experimental-test-coverage --test dist-test/*.js",test/brief.test.ts,project,1800
